Council guidance on windows says that replacement windows in a conservation area need an application unless they match the existing windows in material and pattern. Since 27 Station Road isn't in a conservation area, that specific rule doesn't appear to apply, so replacing the windows may not need planning permission. I can't give a formal opinion on whether your particular works need consent, though. If you're unsure, or if you plan to change the windows' design, materials or size, check with the planning desk before you start.
